"[Execution modes](/guides/execution-modes): explore batch mode for "
"scheduling independent jobs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Extensions to consider {#extensions-to-consider}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Replace the dense solver.** `MAX_DIMENSION` is the ceiling on everything at the $^{48}\\mathrm{Cr}$\n"
"scale, and `np.linalg.eigh` on a dense matrix is why. Building the same projected\n"
"Hamiltonian as a sparse matrix and using an iterative eigensolver such as\n"
"`scipy.sparse.linalg.eigsh`, or a Davidson or selected-CI solver designed for nuclear two-body\n"
"interactions, could support larger subspaces. The practical limit depends on matrix sparsity,\n"
"available memory, and solver convergence, and this tutorial does not benchmark that extension. The SQD addon's `qiskit_addon_sqd.fermion.solve_sci` is not a drop-in substitute: it wraps an\n"
"electronic-structure solver and expects one- and two-body integrals in that form, so the shared\n"
"proton $\\times$ neutron product structure is not sufficient on its own. Using it would mean mapping\n"
"the shell-model interaction of Equation (1) into those integrals and validating the result against the\n"
"exact energies this notebook already computes.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Add batching and subsampling.** The published pooled SQD workflow diagonalizes several independent\n"
"subsamples per iteration and keeps the best. This tutorial uses one batch per iteration, which is\n"
"harmless for the variational bound but does not provide the variance information that indicates whether more shots\n"
"would help.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Excited states and other sectors.** The higher eigenvalues of each subspace Hamiltonian are upper\n"
"bounds on excited states in the same symmetry sector, and running at $M_J \\neq 0$ reaches other\n"
"sectors. The $2^+$ check in Step 1 is already half of this calculation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**A cross-shell model space.** Parity is automatically satisfied inside a single major shell, which\n"
"is why it does no work here. An $sd$-$pf$ space mixes $\\ell$ parities, making parity a genuine\n"
"fourth constraint, one that neither SQD's Hamming-weight repair nor the product\n"
"construction would catch on its own.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"**Odd-mass nuclei.** `reference_determinant` requires an even valence count in each species,\n"
"because a time-reversed paired filling is what forces $M_J = 0$. An odd nucleus needs a\n"
"half-integer $M_J$ target and an unpaired reference.\n"
msgstr ""

